From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: graphics pipelines the boot built are not evicted before a draw has used them (EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES=1 or =mesh), off by default

Switches: EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES=1 (exact "1": every such pipeline) or =mesh (exact "mesh":
only task/mesh pipelines); any other value is off. EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES_FLOOR_MIB=<n>
(optional): kept only while the pool's largest free block (PipelineMemoryGate::GateFree, the
memory gate's own reading) is at least n MiB; unset, 0 or the block unknown: always kept.

Why: EvictUnusedPipelines (every 600 frames) destroys a graphics pipeline unused for 9000 frames.
A pipeline the boot built and no draw has asked for yet has never been "used", so the first check
after frame 9000 destroys nearly all the boot's work. The T151 play session of 13 Nov
(a hand-played session): "Evicted 2278 graphics pipelines unused for 9000 frames, 28 left" at 204.9 s,
with the player still in the first area. From 227 s on, 1,490 graphics pipelines were made again at
first sight ("on disk, not built at boot": the label is wrong for these, 0687 fixes it) and most of
the 386 task/mesh pipelines made during play (those have no kept translation and are translated on
the GPU thread, 18 ms each on average, up to 112 ms). The bursts line up with long frames: 248.7 s
(364 made, worst frame 1,004 ms) and 595-607 s (592 made in two reports, 2.4 s on the GPU thread,
worst frames 3,273 / 1,992 / 1,076 ms).

What: in EvictUnusedPipelines, with the switch on, a pipeline that is not in used_this_session
(no draw has used it since it was built) is skipped, for =mesh only when IsMeshPipeline(). Every
draw's first use goes through CurrentGraphicsPipelineSlowPath, which puts the pipeline in
used_this_session; from then on the 9000-frame rule applies as before. used_this_session and
used_and_evicted (the used list the next boot reads) are not changed by the skip. One log line at
the first eviction check and then at most once per 3600 frames: "EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES=<1|
mesh>: <k> pipelines built at boot and not used yet kept, <e> evicted" (plus "(the pool's largest
free block is under the floor: none kept)" when the floor stopped it).

Cost: memory. The code's own estimate is about 0.45 MB of driver memory per built pipeline, so =1
holds up to about 1 GB that the old rule gave back at 205 s (INFERRED: not measured on the console;
VMA usage did not move at that eviction, so it is host heap). By the end of T151 about 2,000
pipelines were back in the cache anyway (log 773 s: "1994 left"); what =1 keeps on top is the boot
pipelines a session never draws. =mesh keeps only the task/mesh ones (INFERRED: one to two hundred pipelines; 256
task/mesh programs were translated at boot). The floor switch gives the old rule back when the pool is short.

Off (unset or any other value): one load of a static per eviction check (every 600 frames); no
line, nothing else changes. Not in the kept-store stamp (only TranslationSwitches are; this
changes no translation).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 819c9da..246a788 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -1311,6 +1311,37 @@ bool MeshCacheBoot() {
     static const bool on = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE");
     return on;
 }
+
+// EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES: a graphics pipeline the boot built and no draw has used yet is not
+// evicted (EvictUnusedPipelines) while the pool has room. Its "last use" is the boot, so the
+// first check after 9000 frames destroyed nearly all of them: the T151 play session of 13 Nov
+// lost 2,278 of the boot's 2,306 graphics pipelines at 205 s, while the player was still in the
+// first area, and then made 1,490 again at first sight in the next areas (reported as "on disk,
+// not built at boot") plus most of its 386 task/mesh pipelines (no kept translation for those:
+// translated on the GPU thread). "1" (exact): every such pipeline; "mesh" (exact): only task/mesh
+// ones. Once a draw has used it, the 9000-frame rule applies as before. With
+// EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES_FLOOR_MIB=<n> they are kept only while the pool's largest free
+// block (the pipeline memory gate's reading) is at least n MiB; unset, 0 or the block unknown:
+// kept. Unset: as before (one load of a static at each eviction check, every 600 frames).
+enum class KeepBoot : u8 { Off, All, Mesh };
+KeepBoot KeepBootPipelines() {
+    static const KeepBoot mode = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES");
+        if (value == nullptr) {
+            return KeepBoot::Off;
+        }
+        const std::string_view text{value};
+        return text == "1" ? KeepBoot::All : text == "mesh" ? KeepBoot::Mesh : KeepBoot::Off;
+    }();
+    return mode;
+}
+u64 KeepBootFloorBytes() {
+    static const u64 floor = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES_FLOOR_MIB");
+        return value != nullptr ? static_cast<u64>(std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10)) << 20 : u64{0};
+    }();
+    return floor;
+}
 } // Anonymous namespace
 
 bool DropMeshDrawsBeforeBuild() {
@@ -2578,6 +2609,15 @@ void PipelineCache::EvictUnusedPipelines() {
     const u64 cutoff = frame_count - EvictAfterFrames;
     const u64 tick = scheduler.CurrentTick();
     size_t evicted = 0;
+    // EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES: pipelines no draw has used yet stay while the pool has room.
+    const KeepBoot keep_boot = KeepBootPipelines();
+    bool keep_room = false;
+    if (keep_boot != KeepBoot::Off) {
+        const u64 floor = KeepBootFloorBytes();
+        const u64 free = floor != 0 ? PipelineMemoryGate::GateFree() : 0;
+        keep_room = free == 0 || free >= floor;
+    }
+    size_t kept_boot = 0;
     for (auto it = graphics_cache.begin(); it != graphics_cache.end();) {
         GraphicsPipeline* const pipeline = it->second.get();
         if (pipeline == nullptr || pipeline == current_pipeline || !pipeline->IsBuilt() ||
@@ -2585,6 +2625,12 @@ void PipelineCache::EvictUnusedPipelines() {
             ++it;
             continue;
         }
+        if (keep_room && !used_this_session.contains(pipeline) &&
+            (keep_boot == KeepBoot::All || pipeline->IsMeshPipeline())) {
+            ++kept_boot;
+            ++it;
+            continue;
+        }
         if (used_this_session.erase(pipeline) != 0) {
             used_and_evicted.insert(it->first.Hash());
         }
@@ -2602,6 +2648,18 @@ void PipelineCache::EvictUnusedPipelines() {
         it = graphics_cache.erase(it);
         ++evicted;
     }
+    if (keep_boot != KeepBoot::Off) {
+        // At the first check and then at most once per 3600 frames (this runs every 600).
+        static u64 last_frame = 0;
+        if (last_frame == 0 || frame_count - last_frame >= 3600) {
+            last_frame = frame_count;
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                     "EDEN_UP_KEEP_BOOT_PIPELINES={}: {} pipelines built at boot and not used yet "
+                     "kept, {} evicted{}",
+                     keep_boot == KeepBoot::All ? "1" : "mesh", kept_boot, evicted,
+                     keep_room ? "" : " (the pool's largest free block is under the floor: none kept)");
+        }
+    }
     if (evicted == 0) {
         return;
     }
